.TH cullpp 1 "2025" "hull 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cullpp \- interactive Wayland region selector
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cullpp
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBcullpp\fR covers every Wayland output with a translucent overlay and lets the
user drag to select a rectangular region.  On confirmation it prints the region
to stdout.  Snap rectangles may be piped in via stdin; a single click on a snap
rect confirms that region immediately.
.PP
cullpp is a drop-in replacement for \fBslurp\fR with the following additional
capabilities: touch input, crosshair overlay, live dimension display, magnetic
edge-snapping, aspect-ratio lock, move-mode (Space), output auto-snapping,
point mode, extended format specifiers, and a crosshair cursor via the native
\fBwp_cursor_shape_v1\fR protocol.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f\fR \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format string (default: \fB%x,%y %wx%h\fR).
.br
.B %x %y %w %h
 \(en coordinates and size (top-left origin, logical pixels)
.br
.B %X %Y
 \(en right edge (\fIx+w\fR) and bottom edge (\fIy+h\fR)
.br
.B %o
 \(en output name of the output containing the largest share of the selection
.br
.B %l
 \(en label of the matching snap rect (empty if none)
.br
.B %%
 \(en literal percent sign
.TP
\fB\-b\fR \fICOLOR\fR
Background dim color (default: \fB#00000044\fR).
.TP
\fB\-c\fR \fICOLOR\fR
Selection fill color (default: \fB#FFFFFF1A\fR).
.TP
\fB\-s\fR \fICOLOR\fR
Selection border color (default: \fB#4444FFFF\fR).
.TP
\fB\-B\fR \fICOLOR\fR
Snap rect outline color (default: \fB#44FF44BB\fR).
.TP
\fB\-w\fR \fIPX\fR
Selection border width in pixels (default: \fB2\fR).
.TP
\fB\-a\fR \fIW:H\fR
Force aspect ratio.  Example: \fB\-a 16:9\fR.  The selection is always
constrained to this ratio.  Combine with \fBShift\fR (held) for a temporary
1:1 override.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR
Display a live \fIW×H\fR dimension overlay near the selection corner, rendered
with 7-segment style glyphs.
.TP
\fB\-D\fR
Draw full-screen crosshair lines (horizontal + vertical) through the cursor at
all times during the selection, across all outputs.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR
Point mode: output a 1×1 pixel region at the click position.  No drag required.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR
Add all connected Wayland outputs as snap rects, labelled by output name.
Useful for output selection: \fBcullpp \-o \-f "%o"\fR prints the output name.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR
Read snap rects from stdin even if stdin is a TTY.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR
Suppress snap rect highlighting (both outline and hover fill).
.TP
\fB\-T\fR \fIPX\fR
Magnetic edge-snapping threshold in logical pixels (default: \fB10\fR).
When the cursor is within this distance of a snap rect's edge, the selection
edge snaps to it.  Set to \fB0\fR to disable.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show a brief help message and exit.
.SH CONTROLS
.TP
\fBLeft-click drag\fR
Draw a new selection region.
.TP
\fBLeft-click\fR (on snap rect)
Immediately confirm the hovered snap rect.
.TP
\fBRight-click\fR or \fBEscape\fR or \fBq\fR
Cancel selection (exits with code 1).
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Confirm the current dragged selection.
.TP
\fBSpace\fR (hold while dragging)
Switch to move mode: the pointer translates the whole selection instead of
resizing it.
.TP
\fBShift\fR (hold while dragging)
Lock aspect ratio to 1:1 (square).  Overrides \fB\-a\fR temporarily.
.TP
\fBTouch drag\fR
Same semantics as pointer drag.  Only the first touch point is tracked.
.SH STDIN FORMAT
One snap rect per line:
.PP
.RS
\fIx\fR,\fIy\fR \fIW\fRx\fIH\fR [\fIlabel\fR]
.RE
.PP
This is the same format as \fBslurp\fR(1) snap rects.  The label is optional
and available as \fB%l\fR in the format string.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
A region was confirmed.
.TP
\fB1\fR
Selection was cancelled, or an error occurred.
.SH EXAMPLES
Select a region and take a screenshot with grim:
.PP
.RS
.nf
grim \-g "$(cullpp)" screenshot.png
.fi
.RE
.PP
Select a window from Sway's tree:
.PP
.RS
.nf
swaymsg \-t get_tree \\
  | jq \-r '.. | select(.pid? and .visible?) | .rect | "\\(.x),\\(.y) \\(.width)x\\(.height)"' \\
  | cullpp
.fi
.RE
.PP
Select a Wayland output by name:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cullpp \-o \-f "%o"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Select a 16:9 region with live dimensions and crosshair:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cullpp \-a 16:9 \-d \-D
.fi
.RE
.PP
Select a single pixel:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cullpp \-p \-f "%x %y"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR slurp (1),
.BR grim (1),
.BR wf-recorder (1)
.SH AUTHORS
cullpp was written as a drop-in, feature-extended successor to slurp by Simon Ser.
